                    <t:note>      
                        <t:date type="foundation" notBefore="1909" notAfter="1930">According to an additional note in a manuscript, it was established at the foot of the <t:placeName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/LOC2977Entott">ʾƎnṭoṭṭo Mountain</t:placeName> by <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS9345taytuBe">Empress Ṭāytu</t:persName> in 1902 EC. Later, <t:persName ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS6642MananAs">Empress Manan</t:persName> built a new church in 1923 EC. Rās Dastā supervised the construction work.</t:date>
                        <t:ab type="description">Near the church, there is a holy water spring which is highly visited due to the belief of its miraculous healing power. </t:ab>
                        <t:ab type="description" subtype="school">All levels of the ecclesiastical education are offered, even though some of them are not active. According to the information obtained in <t:date notBefore="2020" notAfter="2024">2020-2024</t:date> by the <t:ref target="https://www.aai.uni-hamburg.de/en/ethiostudies/research/abennat.html">ʾAbǝnnat project</t:ref>, the following levels  of traditional education were avaialable: 
